From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Reichel <sebastian.reichel@collabora.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:14:31 +0100
Subject: arm64: dts: rockchip: Fix USBDP ports for Indiedroid Nova

Fix the USBDP PHY ports description for the Indiedroid Nova, so that it
follows the documented ABI. The current binding confuses endpoints with
ports and makes no sense at all.

While at it drop the rockchip,dp-lane-mux property, which makes no sense
for USB-C as the DP lanes are routed dynamically based on negotiation
via the USB-PD protocol.

Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Fixes: 7230cdc1fc3c ("arm64: dts: rockchip: Enable USB-C DP Alt for Indiedroid Nova")
Signed-off-by: Sebastian Reichel <sebastian.reichel@collabora.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261126-rockchip-usb-c-dp-altmode-v1-3-7991eb5bb426@collabora.com
Signed-off-by: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-indiedroid-nova.dts | 31 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-indiedroid-nova.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-indiedroid-nova.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-indiedroid-nova.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-indiedroid-nova.dts
@@ -1044,31 +1044,42 @@ &usbdp_phy0 {
 	mode-switch;
 	sbu1-dc-gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PA0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 	sbu2-dc-gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PA1 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
-	rockchip,dp-lane-mux = <2 3>;
 	status = "okay";
 
-	port {
+	ports {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <0>;
 
-		usbdp_phy0_ss_out: endpoint@0 {
+		port@0 {
 			reg = <0>;
-			remote-endpoint = <&usbc0_ss>;
+
+			usbdp_phy0_ss_out: endpoint {
+				remote-endpoint = <&usbc0_ss>;
+			};
 		};
 
-		usbdp_phy0_ss_in: endpoint@1 {
+		port@1 {
 			reg = <1>;
-			remote-endpoint = <&usb_host0_xhci_ss>;
+
+			usbdp_phy0_ss_in: endpoint {
+				remote-endpoint = <&usb_host0_xhci_ss>;
+			};
 		};
 
-		usbdp_phy0_dp_in: endpoint@2 {
+		port@2 {
 			reg = <2>;
-			remote-endpoint = <&dp0_out_con>;
+
+			usbdp_phy0_dp_in: endpoint {
+				remote-endpoint = <&dp0_out_con>;
+			};
 		};
 
-		usbdp_phy0_dp_out: endpoint@3 {
+		port@3 {
 			reg = <3>;
-			remote-endpoint = <&usbc0_sbu>;
+
+			usbdp_phy0_dp_out: endpoint {
+				remote-endpoint = <&usbc0_sbu>;
+			};
 		};
 	};
 };
-- 
Armbian

From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Reichel <sebastian.reichel@collabora.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:14:32 +0100
Subject: arm64: dts: rockchip: Add USB-C DP AltMode for RK3588 EVB1

Fix the USB-C connector description, so that it follows the binding:

port@0 is the high-speed lanes
port@1 is the super-speed lanes
port@2 is the SBU lanes

This also updates the port naming, so that it describes the hardware
instead of how the drivers are using the information. These are
effectively the same, but the DT should describe hardware and not
software.

Last but not least it now correctly describes the DP side of things,
so that DP AltMode starts working once the kernel has support for it.

Signed-off-by: Sebastian Reichel <sebastian.reichel@collabora.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261126-rockchip-usb-c-dp-altmode-v1-4-7991eb5bb426@collabora.com
Signed-off-by: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
